(Q4) Write a shell script to display elements of an array.
#!/bin/bash
# Script to display elements of an array

# Declare an array
my_array=("red" "green" "blue" "yellow")

# Display all elements at once
echo "All elements: ${my_array[@]}"

# Display elements one by one with their index
echo "Elements with their indices:"
for i in "${!my_array[@]}"
do
  echo "Index $i: ${my_array[$i]}"
done

 






(Q5) What is the purpose of cron in Linux? 
cron is a time-based job scheduler in Linux (and Unix-like systems) that allows users to automatically run scripts or commands at specified times or intervals without manual intervention.
    • Automates repetitive tasks — like backups, updates, system monitoring, sending emails, etc.
    • Runs commands periodically (every minute, hourly, daily, weekly, etc.).
    • Uses crontab files to schedule jobs.
    • Runs tasks in the background (daemon service).
